# Frontend build

When you change anything under `frontend/` (source, `public/`, Vite config, etc.), before finishing the task run a production build from the frontend package:

```bash
cd frontend
npm run build
```

If the build fails, fix the errors and re-run until it passes.

After a **successful** build during agent work, run `git restore frontend/dist` and `git clean -fd frontend/dist/assets` so local hash-renamed assets do not flood Source Control. Do not stage `frontend/dist` unless the user explicitly asks to commit a deploy bundle.

For production deploy, `frontend/dist/` is still built and uploaded (or committed) separately — see `deploy/NGINX_DEPLOY.md`.
